    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205348": {
      "title": "Counseling Services Outreach Assistant (Work Study) 1 Position",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Counseling Services Outreach Assistant (Work Study) 1 Position Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Counseling Services Outreach Assistant (Work Study) 1 Position Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Counseling Services Outreach Assistant (Work Study) 1 Position Category: Work Study Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Sep 30, 2026 Closes: Oct 9, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: PT No Benefits Position ID: 205348 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: Department: Counseling Center Job Title: Counseling Services Outreach Assistant Number of Vacancies: 1 SSTA Supervisor: Julie Glovin Position Type: Non-Supervisory Number of Hours Per Week: 6 General Statement of Duties/Responsibilities: Assist  Counseling Services in social media outreach and the marketing of mental health programs. Contribute to the development and promotion of critical mental health awareness campaigns and resource information. Work collaboratively with Counseling Services staff members. Participate in weekly supervisory meetings. Attend programs as schedule allows to aid marketing, promotion and student outreach. Tabling for Counseling Services resources and programming Assisting with Fresh Check Day  (organizing, outreach to community, planning and running of the event day of, marketing) Requirements: Experience: Comfort with content area and topics of mental health and suicide prevention. Experience in fields related to content (e.g. Sociology, Psychology, Urban Studies, Public Health, Marketing/Communication preferred). - Experience in social media marketing and content creation. - Flexibility in schedule to attend and promote awareness and education programs. - Comfort in engaging peers. - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage diverse groups of students, faculty, and community members. - Experience working in mental  health, advocacy, peer education, or marketing is preferred. - Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. *This position is available for WSU students only* Hourly Rate: $15.00 Application Instructions: Students must apply online. A representative from the department will contact individuals for interviews. *This position is for students WITH WORK STUDY ONLY* Please note - Students may not work during scheduled class time, even if class is cancelled. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    },
    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205346": {
      "title": "Nursing Clerical Assistant (Work Study) 2 Positions",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Nursing Clerical Assistant (Work Study) 2 Positions Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Nursing Clerical Assistant (Work Study) 2 Positions Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Nursing Clerical Assistant (Work Study) 2 Positions Category: Work Study Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Sep 30, 2026 Closes: Oct 9, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: PT No Benefits Position ID: 205346 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: Department: Nursing Job Title: Nursing Clerical Assistant Number of Vacancies: 2 SSTA Supervisor: Tyler Position Type: Non-Supervisory Number of Hours Per Week: 6 General Statement of Duties/Responsibilities: Reception duties: answering telephones, taking/distributing messages, greeting office guests, answering questions, and directing to the proper individual(s). General office duties, such as filing, copying, scanning, data entry, and campus delivery. Other administrative duties or special projects as assigned. Requirements: Experience: Professional and friendly demeanor Basic Microsoft Office skills (Word and Excel) Willingness to learn Experience in an office environment is helpful but not required Must be a federal work study recipient. Non-nursing students preferred Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. *This position is available for WSU students only* Hourly Rate: $15.00 Application Instructions: Students must apply online. A representative from the department will contact individuals for interviews. *This position is for students WITH WORK STUDY ONLY* Please note - Students may not work during scheduled class time, even if class is cancelled. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    }
